{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784538071,"nonce":"xUIvaEFswx6pDBTtY6iRfWwvjcs=","title":"[adr-0056] Engine: tear down orphaned Pod on superseded in-flight attempt","message":"Amends ADR-0056 (the one real engine gap). crates/scarab-engine restart_step re-arms an in-flight descendant Running-\u003ePending (scheduler.rs:161) but never tears down its Pod. Fencing keeps results correct (late verdict rejected) but the Pod runs on as an orphan wasting resources.\n\n- On re-arming an in-flight invalidated step, enqueue an executor teardown (SIGTERM + grace) for its current attempt handle, mirroring reconcile_cancellations.\n- OPTIONAL: emit an explicit AttemptSuperseded { step, attempt } event for audit, so 'superseded' is durable rather than only client-derived.\n\nAcceptance: rerunning b while a descendant is in-flight deletes the descendant's Pod; no orphan. Independent of the UI tickets.","files":null}]}